er wait** is each `ci.yml` job\'s created to started, by the job\'s own creation, for jobs of every attempt that got a runner, each job once (a job carried over from an earlier attempt counts in its own); run time is shown in the CI tables above.\n- Only aggregate numbers are published: no PR, ticket, run or thread numbers, and no comment or log text.\n\n[Journey cohorts, finding kinds, credits and tagged experiments](journey-trends.md).\n\nEvery bench, the CI ones too, in [1-hour and 6-hour buckets](buckets.md), each value with its sample size.\n\n![PRs an hour](prs-per-hour.svg)\n\n![Robot minutes](robot-minutes.svg)\n\n![Time split](time-split.svg)\n\n![Minutes per PR over days](minutes-per-pr.svg)\n\n## Cost and limits\n\nCosts are USD list-rate estimates before included/free minutes, not invoices. GitHub-hosted jobs round each job up to a whole minute; third-party estimates use the same conservative unit. PC compute here is incremental runner-provider spend ($0); electricity, hardware, maintenance and storage are excluded. The proposed self-hosted platform fee is postponed per current GitHub docs. Unknown runner, price or job duration means unknown total, never $0. Backfill records invalid durations in unsuccessful runs as timing gaps; successful-run timing anomalies still fail closed. Cost/code run counts successful code runs only; window cost includes every collected job, including failures, docs-only and scheduled runs. The collection includes the latest attempt of completed CI runs created inside the window; earlier attempts and still-running jobs are not billed here. Re-run a window after it settles. Daily rows use fixed PST, including summer; labelled checkpoints may overlap days and are never added together. A code run is a proxy for one PR: repeated runs and main pushes mean this is capacity, not actual PR throughput. Robots is an explicit capacity assumption; mixed-provider capacity is an estimate. New daily latency is workflow creation to last job completion, an explicit push-to-result proxy: GitHub does not provide the original push-event timestamp here. The historical baseline uses first-job creation instead. Daily capacity uses the supplied robot count as a consistent assumption, not a verified historic fleet size. Missing successful code runs stay unknown and break the daily lines.\n\nSee [bench.md](bench.md) for the reconstructed baseline correction and all timing tables.\n\n| Window | Runner kind | Runner minutes | Billed minutes |\n| --- | --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 2030-01-01 PST | jog-8vcpu | 3.5000 | 3.5 |\n| 2030-01-02 PST | jog-16vcpu | 3.5000 | 3.5 |\n\n| Price kind | Compute/min | Platform/min | Source, verified |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| blacksmith-2vcpu-ubuntu-2404 | $0.0040 | $0.0000 | [2026-11-05](https://www.blacksmith.sh/pricing) |\n| github-hosted | $0.0060 | $0.0000 | [2026-11-05](https://docs.github.com/en/billing/reference/actions-runner-pricing) |\n| github-hosted-slim | $0.0020 | $0.0000 | [2026-11-05](https://docs.github.com/en/billing/reference/actions-runner-pricing) |\n| jog-16vcpu | $0.0088 | $0.0000 | [2026-11-14](https://usejog.com/docs/pricing/) |\n| jog-4vcpu | $0.0024 | $0.0000 | [2026-11-14](https://usejog.com/docs/pricing/) |\n| jog-8vcpu | $0.0044 | $0.0000 | [2026-11-14](https://usejog.com/docs/pricing/) |\n| self-hosted | $0.0000 | $0.0000 | [2026-11-05](https://docs.github.com/en/billing/concepts/product-billing/github-actions) |\n| unknown | unknown | unknown | [2026-11-05](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/workflow-jobs) |\n'

